infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title DI container vs hand-wiring — magic vs explicitness
  desc Same inversion of control — one automates assembly, the other keeps it visible and fast
  compares
    - label DI container
      children
        - label Buys decoupling and a one-line test seam
          desc Assembles the whole object graph; swap an implementation in one spot
        - label Boots in tens to hundreds of ms
          desc Reflects decorator metadata for a few hundred providers at startup
        - label Stings on serverless cold start
          desc That metadata reflection is a measurable slice of a per-millisecond invocation
        - label Stack trace runs through the framework
          desc Resolution internals, not your code, so stepping through is harder
    - label Hand-wiring
      children
        - label Plain new() in one factory function
          desc buildApp() constructs the objects and returns the root
        - label Boots in microseconds
          desc No metadata reflection — direct construction at the edge
        - label Every dependency is go-to-definition
          desc The stack trace runs through your code, not the resolver
        - label Drop it once the graph is small
          desc A CLI, a worker, or a single-purpose Lambda with about five objects
theme
  palette #f59e0b #14b8a6
